prediction.statement:
k_new = 1 for this model. Each baseline in D5 needs k_new >= 8, or never reaches 0.9 at k <= 16. The baselines are:
- the fresh-mode RLS fitted to the B pairs only;
- MesaNet pooled ridge;
- Gated DeltaNet as defined by its equations in D5, with its forgetting factor chosen by oracle maximum over {0.5, 0.7, 0.9, 0.99} separately for each k (D5), which makes this claim conservative;
- the e_t = 1 ablation.

falsifiers:
Pretrain on cyclic-rule episodes, then test on a 26-letter Caesar task with M = 25. Use base shifts s_A coprime to 26 (odd and != 13), so that every nonzero shift is c* s_A mod 26 for a unique c* in {1..25}.

After 24 demonstrations of s_A, measure on the in-context K, without reference to any assumed exact operator:
- eta(K) = max over letters a of ||K^T Phi[a] - Phi[a+s_A mod 26]||;
- rho(K) = ||K||_2;
- E_25(K) = eta(K) * sum_{j=0}^{24} rho(K)^j;
- the margin mu = min(delta_min/2, gamma) of D3, computed on the trained rows.

Also check gate condition (G) on every demonstration pair of the test.

If E_25(K) >= mu in more than 10% of trials, or (G) fails on any test pair, pretraining does not make cyclic rules into a single gated linear flow, which the few-shot argument requires.

Many-rules trace check (reference lift, the 500 trials of the many-rules task).

After every written pair, record:
- the snapped token j_t;
- E_60(K_t);
- ||K_t - (I - lambda P_t) T_A||_2.

In every trial where the base block ends with sigma_min^2 >= 1e-3 (A2), the theory requires:
- each B_i write snaps to j_t = b_i + (c_i* - 1) s_A mod 61;
- E_60(K_t) never exceeds 60 lambda ||P_{t0}|| + 1e-6;
- ||K_t - (I - lambda P_t) T_A||_2 <= 1e-6.

A violation in more than 1% of such trials refutes step (3): transported writes would then accumulate error.
